       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day (about 2,000\u20132,550 mg/day for immediate-release). A dose that high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the max)\n- **1,000 mg twice daily with meals** (2,000 mg/day)\n- **500 mg three times daily with meals** (1,500 mg/day)\n- **1,700 mg per day total**, split into divided doses\n\nTell me the intended dose and frequency and I'll enter it right away. If 1,700 mg three times daily is intentional, tell me and I'll enter it with a note that you confirmed it. I'd still suggest a pharmacist review first."
      }
